WEBVTT

00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:01.899
This is the payments portal for the

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:04.459
orchestrator, Unicity's in-house payment service.

00:00:05.227 --> 00:00:06.934
The Payments team sets it up and runs

00:00:06.977 --> 00:00:08.257
it here, without a developer.

00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:10.134
Nine pages are working today,

00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:11.585
and they do three jobs:

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.718
connect, route, and see.

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:16.706
Job one:

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:17.645
connect.

00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:19.889
Processors is where Payments connects our

00:00:19.931 --> 00:00:20.631
merchant accounts.

00:00:20.998 --> 00:00:21.979
Six are connected today,

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:25.094
across Worldpay, Nuvei, Braintree for

00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:26.630
PayPal, and Network Merchants.

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:29.354
Each one is set up, tested and switched

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:31.658
on here, and adding another takes three

00:00:31.828 --> 00:00:32.528
short steps.

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:36.625
Checkout previews the payment form exactly

00:00:36.881 --> 00:00:37.734
as a shopper sees it.

00:00:38.161 --> 00:00:40.038
Pick a market, and the portal shows that

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:42.214
country's ways to pay and its own address

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.390
layout, at desktop or mobile size.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.938
Settings holds the websites allowed to

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.157
show that form and the keys our servers use.

00:00:51.626 --> 00:00:53.717
Rotating a key never breaks checkout:

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.277
the old key keeps working for twenty-four hours.

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:00.101
Team shows everyone who can sign in.

00:01:00.442 --> 00:01:02.661
An admin invites a teammate by link,

00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:04.623
and everyone has their own login,

00:01:05.007 --> 00:01:06.714
so every change carries a name.

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:09.196
Job two:

00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:10.177
route.

00:01:10.245 --> 00:01:12.293
Routing decides which processor account

00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:13.317
charges each payment.

00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:15.451
Pick a market and a kind of payment,

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:16.517
then build the rules.

00:01:16.985 --> 00:01:19.033
A rule can send everything to one account,

00:01:19.332 --> 00:01:21.209
or split it across several by share,

00:01:21.636 --> 00:01:23.087
with failover to the next account,

00:01:23.428 --> 00:01:25.604
and a fallback for anything no rule matches.

00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:28.959
Before anything is published,

00:01:29.385 --> 00:01:31.689
the portal lists where every card brand

00:01:31.945 --> 00:01:34.079
and wallet would land, and Try a payment

00:01:34.164 --> 00:01:35.871
runs a dry run that charges nothing.

00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:38.516
More than forty dry runs so far,

00:01:38.815 --> 00:01:40.735
and every one went where the rules said.

00:01:41.102 --> 00:01:42.980
Then save a draft, publish,

00:01:43.278 --> 00:01:44.772
and every version is kept.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:47.549
Job three:

00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:48.487
see.

00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:50.305
Payments shows every payment.

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:52.609
Open one, and every attempt is there:

00:01:52.993 --> 00:01:54.102
the processor that took it,

00:01:54.315 --> 00:01:55.015
and how it ended.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.089
This one was paid on its third attempt.

00:01:57.515 --> 00:01:59.563
Orders shows the same payment under our

00:01:59.606 --> 00:02:00.459
own order reference.

00:02:02.266 --> 00:02:04.314
Webhooks are the signed messages that tell

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:06.191
our systems what happened to each payment.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:08.026
Here is the one for that payment:

00:02:08.538 --> 00:02:10.799
delivered, with the reply exactly as

00:02:10.842 --> 00:02:12.463
received, and it can be sent again.

00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:15.815
And the Dashboard adds it all up.

00:02:16.284 --> 00:02:19.441
Pick today, seven, thirty or ninety days,

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.788
and each figure compares itself with the

00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:23.793
period before, including payments that

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:25.159
succeeded after a decline.

00:02:25.624 --> 00:02:27.544
A switch in the header moves every page

00:02:27.715 --> 00:02:28.952
between Test and production.

00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:32.649
That is the payments portal for the

00:02:32.692 --> 00:02:33.392
orchestrator today.

00:02:33.972 --> 00:02:35.892
Payments connects the processor accounts,

00:02:36.276 --> 00:02:38.495
sets, tests and publishes the routing,

00:02:38.836 --> 00:02:41.225
and sees every payment, attempt and

00:02:41.268 --> 00:02:42.905
webhook in one place.

